(2449468, 336818, 50034, '<td valign="top"><b>Thanks for proof!  I''m convinced!</b> <br/>  The composition &amp; concept are both Great!  The colors of the pavement, however, detract from the "sale" of the concept.  As I look closely I see little red specks of sandstone (possibly.)  I''m trying to imagine what this photo might look like if the red channel of the pavement had increased saturation.  Maybe the application of a Warming filter over-all would really "SELL" this photo.<br/>  Of course, if your "bottom line" thought was <i>"It''s so hot today that I could fry an egg on the sidewalk, even in the shade,"</i> then you "nailed it!"  Congratulations!</td>', 'Thanks for proof!  I''m convinced!   The composition & concept are both Great!  The colors of the pavement, however, detract from the "sale" of the concept.  As I look closely I see little red specks of sandstone (possibly.)  I''m trying to imagine what this photo might look like if the red channel of the pavement had increased saturation.  Maybe the application of a Warming filter over-all would really "SELL" this photo.  Of course, if your "bottom line" thought was "It''s so hot today that I could fry an egg on the sidewalk, even in the shade," then you "nailed it!"  Congratulations!', '2006-05-23 11:29:19.000000', NULL, 1),
(2449474, 335862, 51538, '<td valign="top">I always think that head on fire have more symbolic effect than hands on fire.  None-the-less, it is a well executed image.  The symbolism is obscure, though.</td>', 'I always think that head on fire have more symbolic effect than hands on fire.  None-the-less, it is a well executed image.  The symbolism is obscure, though.', '2006-05-23 11:30:24.000000', NULL, 1),
