(2463698, 337403, 16912, '<td valign="top">I like this a lot more second time around than first (second pass I like to spend a little more time)Considering the springs were probably glowing white anyway I think you have done a great job with the exposure and the composition is (for me) spot on. A very clean and simple looking image that was probably a dog to execute (bumping up 1)</td>', 'I like this a lot more second time around than first (second pass I like to spend a little more time)Considering the springs were probably glowing white anyway I think you have done a great job with the exposure and the composition is (for me) spot on. A very clean and simple looking image that was probably a dog to execute (bumping up 1)', '2006-05-28 15:43:57.000000', NULL, 1),
(2463700, 337328, 16912, '<td valign="top">Wow, that is some flame! Normally flames and B&amp;W don''t work but I think you made a bold and wise choice here, I think a colour shot would have lost some detail of the complexity of the flame. The finishing touch for me is the rather nonchalant look of the chef. A good luck bump of +1</td>', 'Wow, that is some flame! Normally flames and B&W don''t work but I think you made a bold and wise choice here, I think a colour shot would have lost some detail of the complexity of the flame. The finishing touch for me is the rather nonchalant look of the chef. A good luck bump of +1', '2006-05-28 15:48:40.000000', NULL, 1),
(2463708, 337392, 16912, '<td valign="top">I''m not a pyromaniac - honestly but I am strangely drawn to flames. This is an excellent closeup and almost abstract. It may be my eyes after looking at this for so long but the match isn''t quite horizontal to me (bumping to an 8).</td>', 'I''m not a pyromaniac - honestly but I am strangely drawn to flames. This is an excellent closeup and almost abstract. It may be my eyes after looking at this for so long but the match isn''t quite horizontal to me (bumping to an 8).', '2006-05-28 15:54:27.000000', NULL, 1),
(2463712, 337102, 16912, '<td valign="top">ooh, I can see travel mags wanting this, so much room for their sales pitch in the negative space. A lovely minimilist approach to the challenge. I may have ''stretched'' the truth with the title though as (to me) sunset has more warmth to me than sunrise? bumping to an eight.</td>', 'ooh, I can see travel mags wanting this, so much room for their sales pitch in the negative space. A lovely minimilist approach to the challenge. I may have ''stretched'' the truth with the title though as (to me) sunset has more warmth to me than sunrise? bumping to an eight.', '2006-05-28 15:59:35.000000', NULL, 1),
(2463715, 337296, 16912, '<td valign="top">Oh yes, I want to try this :) I have seen many shots in this challenge that imho deserve to ribbon and have added this to my list (so you should be in the top ten lol) Good luck (bumping up 1)</td>', 'Oh yes, I want to try this :) I have seen many shots in this challenge that imho deserve to ribbon and have added this to my list (so you should be in the top ten lol) Good luck (bumping up 1)', '2006-05-28 16:02:14.000000', NULL, 1),
(2463731, 337338, 16912, '<td valign="top">ok, I give up! Am thinking some sort of grill over an element? The colours certainly depict warmth/heat and whatever it is (probably something simple?) this is a very good abstract. The repetition of the strong diagonals and colour makes this a great pic that I can picture on somebodies wall as a large print. as a nit picking thought I think I''d have preferred the border to be solid black so the darker areas of the image bled into the bg? A good luck +1 bump.</td>', 'ok, I give up! Am thinking some sort of grill over an element? The colours certainly depict warmth/heat and whatever it is (probably something simple?) this is a very good abstract. The repetition of the strong diagonals and colour makes this a great pic that I can picture on somebodies wall as a large print. as a nit picking thought I think I''d have preferred the border to be solid black so the darker areas of the image bled into the bg? A good luck +1 bump.', '2006-05-28 16:10:40.000000', NULL, 1),
(2463742, 337109, 16912, '<td valign="top">Woodies oft don''t score well here, I think this will be a high scoring woody shot. His posture is great and you can almost see his anguish and their is an air of tension, please tell me no woodies were hurt in the creation of this shot? (bumping 2 after reading my comment lol)</td>', 'Woodies oft don''t score well here, I think this will be a high scoring woody shot. His posture is great and you can almost see his anguish and their is an air of tension, please tell me no woodies were hurt in the creation of this shot? (bumping 2 after reading my comment lol)', '2006-05-28 16:15:25.000000', NULL, 1),
(2463753, 337447, 16912, '<td valign="top">Tut tut, did nobody ever tell you that you should finish your wine before you start your sweet? (pudding wines are normally white). The clarity and sharpness of the foreground is (to me) exceptional! I understand the reason for the ''smoke'' coming from behind the cake but think light use of a blow torch on the chocolate would have had a better effect? A good luck bump of 1 :)</td>', 'Tut tut, did nobody ever tell you that you should finish your wine before you start your sweet? (pudding wines are normally white). The clarity and sharpness of the foreground is (to me) exceptional! I understand the reason for the ''smoke'' coming from behind the cake but think light use of a blow torch on the chocolate would have had a better effect? A good luck bump of 1 :)', '2006-05-28 16:20:33.000000', NULL, 1),
