(2468193, 337416, 28710, '<td valign="top">Wow.<br/> <br/>The scariest thing about this setup to me is that when it''s raining, my butt tends to get wet... even with a fender for some reason..<br/> <br/>Burning gasoline would suck if it sprayed up... YIKES!<br/> <br/>You get an A for Affort though... hmr. that doesn''t quite work.</td>', 'Wow. The scariest thing about this setup to me is that when it''s raining, my butt tends to get wet... even with a fender for some reason.. Burning gasoline would suck if it sprayed up... YIKES! You get an A for Affort though... hmr. that doesn''t quite work.', '2006-05-30 09:56:18.000000', NULL, 0),
(2468202, 337236, 28710, '<td valign="top">Mindblowing... The lighting is my gripe, but there ain''t much you could have done about it without going with a black BG.... That would have changed the early morning feel of the coffee cup with the soft grey setting IMHO...<br/> <br/>This is a fantastic shot without the details, but even more so after reading about it... talk about patience! :)</td>', 'Mindblowing... The lighting is my gripe, but there ain''t much you could have done about it without going with a black BG.... That would have changed the early morning feel of the coffee cup with the soft grey setting IMHO... This is a fantastic shot without the details, but even more so after reading about it... talk about patience! :)', '2006-05-30 10:00:17.000000', NULL, 0),
(2468212, 335862, 28710, '<td valign="top">Oh man! You didn''t think of any tricks to slow the flame down? Now that is hardcore! Maybe using a bit of wax or something on your fingers to protect them? AYEE! I realize that wax is also flammable, but I think it might burn slower and give you a moment to shoot and put it out...<br/> <br/>Take care with those fingers... they are important for camera operation.... and a few other things I think.... Incidentally, there''s quite a large number of nerve endings in our fingertips... I guess you know that pretty well now... :)<br/> <br/>The lighting is really good in this. I am reminded of my own difficulties with a similar setup... Well done.</td>', 'Oh man! You didn''t think of any tricks to slow the flame down? Now that is hardcore! Maybe using a bit of wax or something on your fingers to protect them? AYEE! I realize that wax is also flammable, but I think it might burn slower and give you a moment to shoot and put it out... Take care with those fingers... they are important for camera operation.... and a few other things I think.... Incidentally, there''s quite a large number of nerve endings in our fingertips... I guess you know that pretty well now... :) The lighting is really good in this. I am reminded of my own difficulties with a similar setup... Well done.', '2006-05-30 10:06:11.000000', NULL, 0),
(2468246, 337360, 28710, '<td valign="top">Really nicely done Mel. This was one of my favorites during voting too... It''s a bit soft, so I am guessing that your shutter speed was just a tad slow for it... This translates to ambient light on the cup and of course the aperture too... ISO 200 at f/4 might have helped the fire look a bit brighter, while getting it a bit faster might have brought out some lines... Just an idea... I''m also not a huge fan of the foil... I would probably have gone with pulling the black background down to the bottom instead... for safety, you could have lined the non-visible parts of the BG with foil...</td>', 'Really nicely done Mel. This was one of my favorites during voting too... It''s a bit soft, so I am guessing that your shutter speed was just a tad slow for it... This translates to ambient light on the cup and of course the aperture too... ISO 200 at f/4 might have helped the fire look a bit brighter, while getting it a bit faster might have brought out some lines... Just an idea... I''m also not a huge fan of the foil... I would probably have gone with pulling the black background down to the bottom instead... for safety, you could have lined the non-visible parts of the BG with foil...', '2006-05-30 10:19:09.000000', NULL, 0),
(2468259, 336723, 28710, '<td valign="top">I wonder how many people noticed your hand?<br/> <br/>By the looks of things, you have done all your homework, but didn''t I read somewhere that using alcohol was one of the more dangerous methods?<br/> <br/>I''m no expert... Be careful though, it''s pretty dangerous!</td>', 'I wonder how many people noticed your hand? By the looks of things, you have done all your homework, but didn''t I read somewhere that using alcohol was one of the more dangerous methods? I''m no expert... Be careful though, it''s pretty dangerous!', '2006-05-30 10:24:06.000000', NULL, 0),
